  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#mapping_id_1",
  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The man is mapped as the subject of the violent threat and legal consequence",
  "description": "The text 'If you kill as many as you want our government will put you in jail' is directly overlaid on the image of the man, positioning him as the implied subject of the statement. The visual material (the man) is mapped onto the textual material (the threat and consequence) to create an analogical relationship where the man is being portrayed as the person who could commit the act described in the text, and who would then face the legal consequence. This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent, as it uses the man's appearance (turban, beard) to represent a stereotypical Muslim individual, and maps the text's violent and legal implications onto him.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
